---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title="Hologram Live" description="Run, observe, and extend Hologram locally or across explicitly configured remote boundaries.">
  <div class="home">
    <section class="hero">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Local-first runtime infrastructure</p>
        <h1>The host for <span>living</span> Holograms.</h1>
        <p class="hero-copy">A focused local service, CLI, and desktop app for running Hologram modules locally and connecting to remote authorities without hiding where work happens.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button primary" href={sitePath('/docs/getting-started')}>Start building <span>→</span></a>
          <a class="button secondary" href={sitePath('/docs/architecture')}>Explore architecture</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="terminal" aria-label="Terminal showing Hologram startup">
        <div class="terminal-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>hologram — zsh</span></div>
        <pre><code><span class="prompt">$</span> cargo build --release --locked
<span class="quiet">   Finished release profile</span>

<span class="prompt">$</span> ./target/release/hologram init
initialized ~/.config/hologram/live.toml

<span class="prompt">$</span> ./target/release/hologram start
hologram service started (pid 18442)

<span class="prompt">$</span> ./target/release/hologram status
<span class="ready">ready</span> · 6 modules · node</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="feature-strip" aria-label="Core capabilities">
      <article><span class="feature-number">01</span><h2>Typed boundaries</h2><p>Protobuf/gRPC for native clients and OpenAPI/JSON for browsers.</p></article>
      <article><span class="feature-number">02</span><h2>Supervised state</h2><p>Bounded Kameo actors with explicit links and local supervision.</p></article>
      <article><span class="feature-number">03</span><h2>Observable</h2><p>Structured tracing plus opt-in OTLP traces and RPC metrics.</p></article>
      <article><span class="feature-number">04</span><h2>Desktop ready</h2><p>A Tauri app controls the local service through a managed sidecar.</p></article>
    </section>

    <section class="architecture-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">One explicit path</p>
        <h2>Small kernel. Clear boundaries.</h2>
        <p>The host coordinates lifecycle, routing, authentication, telemetry, and modules. Durable state stays in module storage; network calls cross gRPC or HTTP.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="architecture-map">
        <article class="architecture-node"><span>CLIENTS</span><h3>CLI · Tauri · Browser</h3><p>Native and web clients share capabilities without sharing transport assumptions.</p></article>
        <div class="architecture-arrow">→</div>
        <article class="architecture-node accent"><span>KERNEL</span><h3>Hologram service</h3><p>Configuration, routing, actors, auth, audit, telemetry, and lifecycle.</p></article>
        <div class="architecture-arrow">→</div>
        <article class="architecture-node"><span>MODULES</span><h3>Registry · .holo · History</h3><p>Dependency-ordered capabilities behind stable operation identifiers.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cta-panel">
      <div><h2>Inspect every REST operation.</h2><p>Browse the hosted API guide, then use the self-hosted Scalar reference when your local service is running.</p></div>
      <a class="button primary" href={sitePath('/docs/api-reference')}>Browse API reference <span>→</span></a>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
